From 900ec46e6c2447838348408eb90a7e248308c438 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kyeongpyo Kim <hgichon@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 22:53:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] plugins: add DAOS storage backend

Add a NIXL backend for DAOS, the open-source distributed asynchronous
object store. It moves data between local memory (DRAM_SEG) and DAOS
objects (FILE_SEG) with the DAOS object API rather than the DFS file
layer: one descriptor list becomes one daos_obj_fetch()/daos_obj_update()
through the iod array, and the object API costs 0.0137 ms fixed per
object against 0.63 ms for DFS.

- metaInfo names the pool and container, devId the object (the object id
  is derived from it, so it is stable across restarts), addr the offset;
  offsets map to dkey = addr / 64 MiB, akey = addr % 64 MiB.
- Work runs on a fixed pool (NIXL_DAOS_THREADS); each request borrows a
  DAOS event queue and polls it with a deadline (NIXL_DAOS_EQ_TIMEOUT) so
  a dead engine cannot hang a request. Both settings are read through
  nixl::config.
- VRAM_SEG is advertised only when the DAOS client exports
  daos_obj_fetch_gpu().
- Build: -Ddaos_path points at the DAOS client; skipped with a warning
  when it is absent, an error when requested explicitly. Static builds
  (-Dstatic_plugins=DAOS) are registered in src/core.
- Tests in test/unit/plugins/daos need a live pool and are built but not
  registered with meson test.

Tested against a DAOS 2.8.0 server (1 rank, ofi+tcp): the three tests
pass. Built on Ubuntu 24.04 against a DAOS 2.8.0 client built from source.
Throughput, measured with the same backend code on an earlier NIXL and a
DAOS 2.9.100 development build, 2 ranks, 400G verbs: 34.17 GB/s reading
4.69 GiB.

